<title>UK: UK approves Stagecoach moves on Ayrshire.</title>
<headline>UK approves Stagecoach moves on Ayrshire.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British department of trade and industry said on Monday that it had accepted undertakings from Stagecoach Holdings to remedy effects on competition linked to its planned acquisition of Ayrshire Bus Owners Ltd.  </p>
<p>The undertakings would restrict Stagecoach's ability to exploit the strength of its postion by raising fares and cutting services .</p>
<p>Stagecoach had agreed to abide by the recommendations made by the Monopolies and Mergers Commission after a UK court dismissed a Stagecoach petition in June 1996, which challenged the MMC recommendations.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
